{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Versioned named areas for the Grodno Guide. Single source for area resolution (RU/EN names + aliases) and for the project-area geofence predicate (agent.areas.in_project_area, re-exported by agent.geofence.inside_project_area). Geometry is referenced from the border files in this directory, never duplicated and never invented: areas whose boundary polygon does not exist in data/ carry geometry=null, and containment for them is unknown (agent.areas.area_contains returns None) — an explicit unknown, never a silent default.",
  "notes": [
    "District names are taken verbatim from the district column of places_region.csv; English district names are literal translations of the official Russian names.",
    "grodno-oblast geometry is the geoBoundaries ADM1 polygon (grodno_border.json, Creative Commons Attribution 3.0), loaded at runtime from that file.",
    "District geometry is the OSM admin_level=6 ring of that district in districts_border.json (its record named by slug), loaded at runtime from that file: shapes, not bounding boxes, so a district that surrounds the city of Grodno keeps the city a hole.",
    "Boundary exceptions (points treated as inside the project area although they fall outside a border polygon) are the documented keep-list in belarus_border_keep.json; they are loaded into the grodno-oblast definition at runtime.",
    "grodno-old-town has no boundary in OSM, so its polygon is authored here: the convex hull of the curated Grodno objects the quarter holds, buffered 100 m (source in old_town_border.json says so, and the file is versioned data like the rest)."
  ],
